Package: thresholdr
Title: Estimate Optimal Probability Classification Thresholds for
    Diagnostic Models
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("W. Jake", "Thompson", , "wjakethompson@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-7339-0300")),
    person("Jonathan A.", "Pedroza", role = "aut"),
    person("Andrew", "Heiss", role = "cph",
           comment = "shapes_to_muphi() and muphi_to_shapes()"),
    person("University of Kansas", role = "cph")
  )
Description: Diagnostic classification models are confirmatory latent
    class models that provide probabilities of proficiency for respondents
    on each of the assessed skills (Bradshaw, 2016
    <doi:10.1002/9781118956588.ch13>). Often, results based on these
    models are reported as classifications, using 0.5 as the probability
    threshold for classification (Bradshaw & Levy, 2019
    <doi:10.1111/emip.12247>). Instead, this package estimates an optimal
    classification threshold for each skill, even when respondents' true
    classifications are unknown. Thresholds can be approximated by
    resampling plausible classifications or by iterating toward a
    self-consistent threshold, and optimized using a range of criteria
    derived from the receiver operating characteristic curve.
